rectly on intestinal smooth muscle to reduce motility. Clinical outcomes from this combination show treatment durations of 3–7 days (average 4.2 days), indicating synergistic efficacy. This interaction exemplifies rational polypharmacy in acute infectious diarrhea, where symptom control and mucosal healing are pursued simultaneously. The documented interaction reinforces the interconnectedness of pharmacologic agents within this community. [Data: Entities (4691); Relationships (38174, 21466)]\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"消化性溃疡 presents a contraindication context for acid-suppressing therapies\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Although 消化性溃疡 is not directly treated by the primary drugs in this community, it plays an important contextual role due to a documented contraindication. Specifically, 艾普拉唑—a potent gastric acid inhibitor—is contraindicated for long-term, high-dose use in 消化性溃疡 because of its strong acid-suppressing effect. This highlights a critical safety consideration in ulcer management and contrasts with the mucosal-protective approach seen with 思密达-containing regimens. While 消化性溃疡 is peripherally connected, its inclusion underscores the broader landscape of gastrointestinal therapeutics and the importance of avoiding inappropriate pharmacologic interventions. [Data: Entities (16401); Relationships (7197)]\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Traditional Chinese medicines play a notable role in IBS management\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Both 神曲 and 土木香—traditional Chinese medicinal substances—are indicated for 肠易激综合征. 神曲 has demonstrated measurable effects on gut microbiota composition in clinical studies, while 土木香 is cited in literature as a therapeutic option for IBS, though with less detailed mechanistic evidence provided in the source data. Their inclusion alongside modern pharmaceuticals like 丽珠肠乐 and 思密达 illustrates an integrative approach to managing functional gastrointestinal disorders in clinical 